      "text": "Functional Requirements \n\nThese specify the concrete capabilities of the system.\n\n1.  Local-First AI Agent:  The core Goose LLM agent must run entirely on the local NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano\nhardware/Raspberry Pi 5 + AI Hat+ 2\n\n2.  Offline Voice Interaction:\n     The system must have a custom wake-word function that operates without an internet connection.\n     It must perform real-time, on-device speech-to-text and text-to-speech.\n\n3.  Smart Device Control:\n    The system must be able to control a variety of smart home devices (lights, plugs, media).\n     It must support devices both with and without official SDKs, implying the need for direct protocol\nintegration\n     (e.g., Zigbee, LIRC,MQTT and Matter(the standard)) and potentially reverse-engineered controls (Moonbeam\nMCP).\n\n4.  Mobile Companion App (\"Goose on the Go\"):\n     A mobile application must be developed for Android and also iOS.***pls,frameworks we'll use/Mobile Native\n     The app will serve as a remote control and interface for the local hub.\n     It must enable secure, sandboxed control of other mobile apps to extend its capabilities.***\n\n5.  Memory and Self-Improvement:\n    The agent must have a memory system to recall past interactions and user preferences.\n     It must incorporate a feedback loop to allow for self-improvement over time (as described by the \"self-\nrewriting prompt system\").\n\n6.  Multi-Platform Support: \nThe core software stack must be designed to be portable, running on both the main \"Pond\" hardware and the\n\"Goose on the Go\" mobile platform.\n\n7. Automation and Scheduling: Goose In A pond will monitor environments and other factors to think through\nand automate tasks, in addition to recognition of faces and giving personalized automated experiences.",
      "fontSize": 26.668335096168153,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements \n\nThese specify the concrete capabilities of the system.\n\n1.  Local-First AI Agent:  The core Goose LLM agent must run entirely on the local NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano hardware/Raspberry Pi 5 + AI Hat+ 2\n\n2.  Offline Voice Interaction:\n     The system must have a custom wake-word function that operates without an internet connection.\n     It must perform real-time, on-device speech-to-text and text-to-speech.\n\n3.  Smart Device Control:\n    The system must be able to control a variety of smart home devices (lights, plugs, media).\n     It must support devices both with and without official SDKs, implying the need for direct protocol integration\n     (e.g., Zigbee, LIRC,MQTT and Matter(the standard)) and potentially reverse-engineered controls (Moonbeam MCP).\n\n4.  Mobile Companion App (\"Goose on the Go\"):\n     A mobile application must be developed for Android and also iOS.***pls,frameworks we'll use/Mobile Native\n     The app will serve as a remote control and interface for the local hub.\n     It must enable secure, sandboxed control of other mobile apps to extend its capabilities.***\n\n5.  Memory and Self-Improvement:\n    The agent must have a memory system to recall past interactions and user preferences.\n     It must incorporate a feedback loop to allow for self-improvement over time (as described by the \"self-rewriting prompt system\").\n\n6.  Multi-Platform Support: \nThe core software stack must be designed to be portable, running on both the main \"Pond\" hardware and the \"Goose on the Go\" mobile platform.\n\n7. Automation and Scheduling: Goose In A pond will monitor environments and other factors to think through and automate tasks, in addition to recognition of faces and giving personalized automated experiences.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
