      "text": "\n\n\nNon-Functional Requirements (How the system will be)\n\nThese define the qualities and constraints of the system.\n\n1.  Privacy-First:\nAll user data, including voice commands, conversations, and device states, must be processed and\nstored locally on the user's hardware.\nNo data should be sent to the cloud by default.\nComponents follow Zero trust rules!\n\n2. Modularity/ Potability:\n The system must be built with a modular architecture (OS, Shell, Goose Agent, UI/UX ). This\nallows for independent development, updates, and community contributions. Develop once compile for\nall. (ARM - NVIDIA TEGRA, METAL, x86 -INTEL, NVIDIA TEGRA etc ...)\n\n3. Performance:\n     The local LLM must achieve a near-real-time response rate, specified in the proposal as 40-70\ntokens per second for 1-7B parameter models.\n     Voice recognition and wake-word detection must have low latency to feel responsive.\n\n4.  Open Source: \nThe entire software stack developed for the project must be open-source to encourage community\nparticipation and transparency.\n\n5.  Usability/ Ease of Use: \nThe interfaces (voice, mobile, web) should be intuitive and provide a seamless user experience for a\ngeneral-purpose assistant. (Consistent, Clear, Easy to Use, Easy to Install and Helpful)\n\n6. Explicit user consent:\nThe system will always seek for permission from the user where applicable to automate tasks and\ncarry forward objectives\n\n7. tactile user feedback: the user should always be in knowledge of the state of the system and\nwhat the system is doing, and the system will PROACTIVELY inform the user",
      "fontSize": 31.894589103031553,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\n\nNon-Functional Requirements (How the system will be)\n\nThese define the qualities and constraints of the system.\n\n1.  Privacy-First:\nAll user data, including voice commands, conversations, and device states, must be processed and stored locally on the user's hardware.\nNo data should be sent to the cloud by default.\nComponents follow Zero trust rules!\n\n2. Modularity/ Potability:\n The system must be built with a modular architecture (OS, Shell, Goose Agent, UI/UX ). This allows for independent development, updates, and community contributions. Develop once compile for all. (ARM - NVIDIA TEGRA, METAL, x86 -INTEL, NVIDIA TEGRA etc ...)\n\n3. Performance:\n     The local LLM must achieve a near-real-time response rate, specified in the proposal as 40-70 tokens per second for 1-7B parameter models.\n     Voice recognition and wake-word detection must have low latency to feel responsive.\n\n4.  Open Source: \nThe entire software stack developed for the project must be open-source to encourage community participation and transparency.\n\n5.  Usability/ Ease of Use: \nThe interfaces (voice, mobile, web) should be intuitive and provide a seamless user experience for a general-purpose assistant. (Consistent, Clear, Easy to Use, Easy to Install and Helpful)\n\n6. Explicit user consent:\nThe system will always seek for permission from the user where applicable to automate tasks and carry forward objectives\n\n7. tactile user feedback: the user should always be in knowledge of the state of the system and what the system is doing, and the system will PROACTIVELY inform the user",
